.TH KAGI-VOLUME-NBD 1 "September 2026" "Kagi 0.38.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-nbd \- expose an object-backed Kagi volume over NBD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-volume-nbd
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Presents a sparse Kagi logical volume as an NBD block endpoint. Read/write/flush/trim operations are translated into volume-range operations against the authoritative Kagi extent map. Whole-extent trim can deallocate extents.
.SH NOTES
NBD is a transport/backend mechanism. Guest-facing presentation should normally be virtio-scsi or virtual SAS/SCSI through the hypervisor. NBD cannot itself carry arbitrary guest SCSI Persistent Reservation CDBs.
.SH SEE ALSO
kagi-volume-qemu-scsi(1), kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi(1), kagi-volume-iscsi-export(1)
